GNU/Emacs Operating System (GEOS)

This file lists the maintainer of GEOS, the cryptographic identity
used to sign releases, commits, and security advisories, and the
per-file-category licensing of everything in the distribution.

================================================================
maintainer
================================================================

Borja Tarraso <borja.tarraso@member.fsf.org>
        also reachable as <borja.tarraso@gmail.com>

GPG signing key (used for git commits, release tags, advisories):

        4491 8A01 3087 BBF8 4D41  C229 4FD9 DE40 1BD9 C40C

To verify a signed commit:

        git log --show-signature

Imports of the public key are available from the usual public
keyservers (keys.openpgp.org, keyserver.ubuntu.com).  When in doubt,
fetch by fingerprint, not by email.

================================================================
authorship and copyright
================================================================

With the exception of the verbatim license texts in category (6)
below, which are published by the Free Software Foundation, every
file in this distribution was written by the maintainer, who is also
the sole copyright holder of every commit in the repository to date.
The maintainer, the copyright holder, and the author are the same
person here; the copyright notices in the files name the copyright
holder.

No file references generative tooling, vendor names behind such
tooling, or any "generated", "co-authored", or "with help from"
attribution phrasing.  The forbidden-token list is enforced by the
repository's pre-commit attribution scan.

If you contribute a patch, sign your work under the
Developer Certificate of Origin (DCO) by adding a Signed-off-by line
to your commit.  See docs/CONTRIBUTING.md for the full process.

================================================================
license, per file category
================================================================

Every file in this distribution falls into one of the categories
below.  Each category has a single, explicit license; that license
applies to every file in the category.

  (1) Source code: .el, .c, .h, .scm, .sh, .yml, .py, .conf, .mk,
      .gitignore, and every file named "Makefile".  Licensed under
      the GNU General Public License, version 3 or later
      (GPL-3.0-or-later).  Each such file carries an
      SPDX-License-Identifier header AND the complete GPL notice
      paragraph in the file's own comment style.  Canonical license
      text in COPYING at the repository root.

  (2) Manuals: docs/USER_GUIDE.md, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md,
      docs/INTERNALS.md, docs/INSTALL.md, docs/HURD_PORT.md,
      docs/HURD_BOOT.md, docs/MANIFESTO.md.  Licensed under the GNU
      Free Documentation License, version 1.3 or later
      (GFDL-1.3-or-later), with no Invariant Sections, no Front-Cover
      Texts, and no Back-Cover Texts.  Each manual states its title,
      author, and copyright on its title page (just after the title,
      where the FDL ADDENDUM says the notices belong) and carries the
      unaltered license notice from the FDL's ADDENDUM there, so a
      manual copied out of the tree alone still names its author and
      its license.  Each manual also includes a complete copy of the
      FDL in its section entitled "GNU Free Documentation License".
      The same license text also ships as COPYING.DOC at the
      repository root.

  (3) Other documentation: every other .md file in the tree (README,
      CHANGELOG, docs/runlogs/*.md, development plans, project
      notes).  These are small supporting files and rough
      documentation in the sense of the GNU maintainers' guide, and
      are released under the all-permissive license (SPDX: FSFAP):
      copying and distribution of these files, with or without
      modification, are permitted in any medium without royalty
      provided the copyright notice and the license notice are
      preserved.  Each such file carries the notice in a visible
      "license" section.

  (4) Upstream patches: docs/upstream/patches/*.patch.  Patches
      written by the maintainer against upstream projects (currently
      a single patch against GNU Emacs).  Each patch carries its
      copyright and GPL license notice appended at the end of the
      file, after the diff, where it does not interfere with
      "git am" or "git apply"; the Emacs patch is GPL-3.0-or-later,
      the same license as the program it modifies.

  (5) Upstream-correspondence drafts: docs/upstream/emails/*.txt.
      Drafts of messages the maintainer wrote and sent to upstream
      mailing lists (bug-hurd, debian-hurd, bug-gnu-emacs).  Released
      under the all-permissive license (FSFAP), with the notice
      appended at the end of each file.

  (6) License texts: COPYING (GNU GPL version 3, verbatim) and
      COPYING.DOC (GNU FDL version 1.3, verbatim), plus the copy of
      the FDL embedded in each manual of category (2).  These texts
      are published by the Free Software Foundation; they were not
      written by the maintainer, and everyone is permitted to copy
      and distribute verbatim copies of them, but changing them is
      not allowed.

  (7) Binary media: docs/img/*.png and docs/runlogs/*.png.
      Inventoried per-file in docs/MEDIA.md with origin and license,
      with the copyright and license notices repeated in a README in
      each directory that holds images (docs/img/README.md and
      docs/runlogs/README.md), so an image copied out of the tree
      alone keeps its notice. All maintainer-made (logos and serial-
      console screenshots), copyright (C) 2025-2026 Borja Tarraso, and
      released under the all-permissive license (FSFAP).

  (8) Project metadata: AUTHORS (this file).  Released under the
      all-permissive license (FSFAP); see the notice at the end of
      this file.

================================================================
license, for redistributors
================================================================

A distributor wishing to repackage GEOS should:

  - keep COPYING and COPYING.DOC at the root of the redistribution
    (they are the license texts the per-file notices refer to);
  - preserve the copyright notices, SPDX headers, full notice
    paragraphs, and "license" sections on the files that carry them;
  - preserve docs/MEDIA.md and the per-directory image READMEs, which
    carry the copyright and license notices for the image files, where
    a notice cannot be embedded in the file itself.

The contribution policy in CONTRIBUTING.md asks every contributor to
sign off under the Developer Certificate of Origin (a Signed-off-by
trailer on each commit); patches without a sign-off will not be merged.
The maintainer holds the copyright and does not require copyright
assignment to the FSF.

